{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474449-reasonable-scaling-of-challenges-for-players","id":1474449,"title":"Reasonable scaling of challenges for players","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-11T15:51:07-08:00","id":1474449,"title":"Reasonable scaling of challenges for players","content":"After 20 years of wanting to run one, finally kicking off a MtA Chronicle. One thing I'm finding particularly challenging, as the title suggests, is scaling challenges for my players so that they're difficult enough for them to have fun and feel accomplished when they overcome them, but not so easy/daunting that the whole story gets bogged down with a mix of boredom and frustration.<br /> <br /> I'm finding this especially difficult when it comes choosing antagonists to throw at them. It's not like a D&amp;D Monster Manual that comes along with handy Challenge Ratings. I mean, obviously a group of 3 Initiates shouldn't be expected to survive a fight with a Rank 5 Abyssal, but there's gotta be a way to balance the scale between pushover and game ender.<br /> <br /> Appreciate any and all advice here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T16:19:30-08:00","id":1474452,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, I feel as though a starting approach of setting things up for direct fights is not the best suited to Chronicles games in general and Mage in particular. I think you might get more traction from the presentation of antagonistic forces that are causing supernatural afflictions or interferences on subjects that are of importance to the player characters, and then letting the story be about how they discover the nature of those things, use their own powers to deal with them, and then trace them back to a source that can be carefully analysed and then have a plan for dealing with going in.<br /> <br /> I think when done that way, the direct confrontation's innate difficulty doesn't exactly matter. If it's weak, then there have been challenges surrounding it and in the process of leading up to it, and then the final phase is what they want to do and how to implement it. If it's strong, it can be about figuring out its possible weaknesses or a creative way to apply powers to confine or redirect it, and then trying that out. <br /> <br /> Like, your Rank 5 gulmoth is very strong sure, but it will have a Bane that, although rare and esoteric, can immediately destroy it. That story shouldn't be about the Initiates going to fight it directly but engaging in a lot of research, deal making, and communing with strange sources of knowledge to learn what the entity's Bane is and undertake to acquire it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:31:08-08:00","id":1474457,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Isator. I was already starting to lean in that direction. and you clarified things for me nicely. My takeaway is less smashy smash and more unveiling of dark mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T18:52:35-08:00","id":1474466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shemihazazel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1474449-reasonable-scaling-of-challenges-for-players?p=1474457#post1474457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Isator. I was already starting to lean in that direction. and you clarified things for me nicely. My takeaway is less smashy smash and more unveiling of dark mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which can lead to a crazy plan where they gather allies, resources and throw everything including the Supernal kitchen sink at their foes. Combat may very well be part or a highlight of it, but doing the information gathering, diplomacy, rare resource hunting and games of intrigue all build up to the big satisfying encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}